Subject: [PATCH] windows.globalization: GeographicRegion, Language names, user
 preferences

GeographicRegion: created from a two-letter, three-letter or numeric ISO 3166
code (E_INVALIDARG for anything else), Code, CodeTwoLetter, CodeThreeLetter,
CodeThreeDigit, DisplayName, NativeName (the region's own language) and
CurrenciesInUse. Language: DisplayName, NativeName and Script. GlobalizationPreferences:
Calendars, Clocks, Currencies and WeekStartsOn from the user's locale. Every object
answers GetIids, GetRuntimeClassName and GetTrustLevel. Removes the todo_wine marks
that now pass.

